    PySide6/cv2 unavailable; verified via py_compile + pyflakes only.) Also review the layout vs the Videos tab
    (this build embeds its own queue list on the left rather than using the drawer listbox) and adjust if desired.
[ ] Add an "All" tab that presents videos AND still images together in a single, ordered, one-at-a-time
    play/record queue — looking and functioning exactly like the current Videos tab, but able to preview
    still images as well as play videos. For workflows where videos and images are meant to be handled in
    sequence in one queue rather than in the separate Videos/Images tabs.
    Where things live today (vat/ui/app.py, the right_panel QTabWidget):
    - Tabs are indexed 0=Videos, 1=Images, 2=Review. The Videos play/record interface is built ~L866-991;
      the Images tab ~L993-1166. Adding a tab SHIFTS these indices — update the hardcoded assumptions in
      _on_tab_changed (~L1183: "0=Videos,1=Images,2=Review"; enables video_listbox only on idx==0) and the
      setTabText(0/1/2,...) block (~L1254). Prefer looking tabs up by reference instead of magic indices.
