      wav_path_for() (<stem>.wav), image -> wav_path_for_image() (<fullname>.wav). For the "has a recording?"
      badge/enable state and for delete/play mapping, use the CANONICAL name only (os.path.exists) — do NOT use
      the loose find_existing_image_audio() stripped-basename fallback inside the All tab: for a same-stem
      video+image pair it can return the video's <stem>.wav and mis-map / delete it. Canonical-only keeps video
      (<stem>.wav) and image (<fullname>.wav) distinct, so same-stem kits are safe without touching the existing
      tabs. The full uniform-naming redesign (below, in the Roadmap) is deferred.
